This assertion asserts that when x is added to the array list, last index of x is greater than or equal to index of x in the old array list. This is the conclusion we need to reach from the test cases.--------------------Debug.Assert statements can be used to check assumptions about the inputs or outputs of the methods that are being tested. Please note that these statements are not guaranteed to be executed in cases when the Assert.True function is False (e.g., when the test is running in Non-Release configuration). 

```cs
[Test]
[PexMethod]
public void PUT_AddContract([PexAssumeUnderTest] ArrayList arrList, int x)
{
    // Assume that true is always true.
    AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);

    int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int Old_x = x;
    int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    int New_Ret = arrList.Add(x);

    int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    // Assert that New_arrListLastIndexOfX >= Old_arrListIndexOfX
    Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX >= Old_arrListIndexOfX);

    // Add more assertions if needed...
}
```

Each test method should have an assert statement placed at the end of the method to ensure that the method's expected outputs are correct and as expected by the method's pre- and post-conditions.

Please note that it's recommended to use Debug.Assert instead of regular assert statements for checking the program flow during testing. The reason being that regular assertions, that end with Assert.True, are only enforced when the test is run in Release configuration while Debug.Assert statements can be disabled by simply having a comment at the line, they can be turned off or on depending on the compilation mode.--------------------There are no comments that start with "@@@" in the given C# code snippet. The assert statements are not present. They would be typically located right after the code that needs to be tested and they would provide feedback about the state of the system.--------------------